  "title": "Material Nesting Best Practice: Reducing Left Over Materials",
  "summary": "Nesting is the process of arranging or fitting together parts in a way to reduce leftover materials. Basically, it's the act of fitting two or more pieces into one larger piece. We always want to optimize our sheet material usage and reduce leftover materials, so in this blogpost we will show you how nesting can help with this.",
